gned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(1)(6)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-8}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102773/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a453400-6363-5782-b346-aae37570c9bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102773"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40429/selection/47ee0fb1fc99fb4702b5f5fe47ba4a74ec35f652ce0100885b8cdfc06d517ee4" :answer/id #uuid "c6e90a35-c8a9-54c4-9c09-319238d91f48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40429/selection/7304e45403a258c572b59ea9b6c5a54f20b0c097a2fea2754d132cebe6963d30" :answer/id #uuid "da01585a-0eb6-585a-aaa6-b338af6407ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =-1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40429/selection/6f85ebe59d51ef6860e59d69b12911556754eda3dd8a97f51b473e338ada8bf8" :answer/id #uuid "1d8401cd-fee5-5bc8-9ed8-db04ca1b5d26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =-2\\pm 3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40429/selection/0f1acc6bb449b103786a461ec60d18a394cab0a48a28557ecc84591693afe953" :answer/id #uuid "ffeaf430-8394-59e8-97e4-947b56ce7c33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =2\\pm 3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40429/selection/9dc9e32e8c07cb55713aac967947119eba89184004a29831ec6bd66540436519" :answer/id #uuid "e3e1b2b5-a8e7-581c-8887-68f2abad689d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40429/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbdd8dc-682b-587b-ac8b-09679c629cb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40429/selection/0f1acc6bb449b103786a461ec60d18a394cab0a48a28557ecc84591693afe953" :answer-field/choices ["q-40429/selection/47ee0fb1fc99fb4702b5f5fe47ba4a74ec35f652ce0100885b8cdfc06d517ee4" "q-40429/selection/7304e45403a258c572b59ea9b6c5a54f20b0c097a2fea2754d132cebe6963d30" "q-40429/selection/6f85ebe59d51ef6860e59d69b12911556754eda3dd8a97f51b473e338ada8bf8" "q-40429/selection/0f1acc6bb449b103786a461ec60d18a394cab0a48a28557ecc84591693afe953" "q-40429/selection/9dc9e32e8c07cb55713aac967947119eba89184004a29831ec6bd66540436519"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40429" :question/id #uuid "d73a0002-f223-52d5-994d-c6e2237466e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-40429" :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\left|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\\right| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-3(-3) & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(1)(13)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-36}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 6\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm 3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40429/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a453400-6363-5782-b346-aae37570c9bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40429"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/va