] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39186" :question/id #uuid "252141a6-142d-5ad2-94ac-bb05b0444744" :question/math-academy-id "q-39186" :question/problem "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4(-2) & =0 \\\\ 5-\\lambda -5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4(1)(13)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39186/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a453400-6363-5782-b346-aae37570c9bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39186"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81022/selection/2675322150a36c43a48e42203169d79b599e603b77c62eac48e8520fe853fe22" :answer/id #uuid "256bf942-98b4-5efa-bf37-8fc7cd6b7d1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =-2\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81022/selection/8415741e1bec464747625fe14fcf7a3d998cfa9f180a9176c37f8719a6d04d5f" :answer/id #uuid "be99cefb-597b-5af2-9bf6-82d0d0ce0085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81022/selection/e3c1b58920f85a5f0b5ecd33563b3956a5ec398d534516cbb